<title>JAPAN: Japan Mar M2+CD money supply up 2.7 pct yr/yr-BO.</title>
<headline>Japan Mar M2+CD money supply up 2.7 pct yr/yr-BO.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's broadly defined money supply average of M2 plus certificates of deposit (CDs) grew a preliminary 2.7 percent in March from a year earlier, the Bank of Japan (BOJ) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The BOJ also said the money supply average grew a preliminary 3.0 percent in the January-March period from the same period last year.  </p>
<p>A breakdown of March money supply figures follows:</p>
<p>(Year-on-year percentage changes)</p>
<p>			    MAR PRELIM  FEB REVISED</p>
<p>Unadjusted M2 + CDs     +2.7	 +3.0</p>
<p>   M1			 +9.5	 +9.8</p>
<p>   CDs		     +11.7	+29.8</p>
<p>			     MAR PRELIM   FEB REVISED</p>
<p>Broadest money measure  +3.6	 +3.8</p>
<p>(Annualised month-on-month percentage changes)</p>
<p>			     MAR PRELIM   FEB REVISED</p>
<p>Adjusted M2 + CDs	 -0.1	 +0.2</p>
<p>(Average outstanding yen levels)</p>
<p>			    MAR PRELIM  FEB REVISED</p>
<p>Unadjusted M2+CDs    563.1 trln   558.7 trln</p>
<p>   M1		    176.5 trln   169.4 trln</p>
<p>   CDs		    19.9 trln    16.7 trln</p>
<p>			    MAR PRELIM  FEB REVISED</p>
<p>Broadest liquidity 1,140.2 trln 1,136.2 trln</p>
<p>A breakdown of January-March money supply figures follows:</p>
<p>(Year-on-year percentage changes)</p>
<p>			    JAN-MAR PRELIM  OCT-DEC REVISED</p>
<p>Unadjusted M2 + CDs     +3.0	 +3.4</p>
<p>   M1			+ 9.8	+10.6</p>
<p>   CDs		     +28.2	+48.5</p>
<p>			     JAN-MAR PRELIM JAN-MAR REVISED</p>
<p>Broadest money measure  +3.7	 +3.6</p>
</text>
